restart-server leaks file descriptors across its execve: fds outside the keepOpenAcrossExec set ride into every successor image. Found live: server pid 3582454 (running the production binary, which has NO ghc-debug stub) still held two ghc-debug LISTEN sockets on fd 50 and fd 55, inherited from earlier -fghc-debug images. Nothing accepts on them, so ghc-debug-brick connects, lands in the backlog (Recv-Q 2) and hangs forever. Narrow fix: CLOEXEC on the stub socket. General fix: cmdReload already names the fds to KEEP (keepOpenAcrossExec, Server.hs ~2057) -- sweep the complement and set CLOEXEC, so no future fd leaks the same way. Same family as the reapMonitor orphan. | id:8a70dc31eda8811c90ac58437fa2932f857f394f
